{"repo_name":"MatterHackers/agg-sharp","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-26T20:20:07Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"162b1f44e3730bdba005f2c6c19c73b2c94c80d2","github_link":"https://github.com/MatterHackers/agg-sharp/commit/162b1f44e3730bdba005f2c6c19c73b2c94c80d2","commit_subject":"Dilate takes manifold-sharp's parallel union tree for a non-convex part: MinkowskiProcessing tries Manifold.TryDilateByConvex before the sweep and falls back when it declines, counting tree runs as a path signal; MinkowskiProgressModel.TreeTimeFraction maps the tree's units onto the clock - the leaves linearly, then each pairwise level weighted by its rounds of unions on the available cores and a per-union cost that grows toward the top, then the closing pass - while erosion keeps the sweep mapping, and the adapter's high-water mark absorbs out-of-order reports from worker threads. The G203 part (46854 triangles, radius 5, 12 segments) dilates in 76-81 s in Release instead of about 8 minutes, and its time-left text no longer sits on one value for 40 s at the end. manifold-sharp also fixes a DedupeEdges defect that could drop solid from a NoError boolean","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"jondgoodwin/cone","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-26T20:20:07Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"d6bfb5b73d4c0bc226c49f2e502ee118452e23f5","github_link":"https://github.com/jondgoodwin/cone/commit/d6bfb5b73d4c0bc226c49f2e502ee118452e23f5","commit_subject":"A borrow held in a local freezes its source until its last use","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"ClickHouse/ClickHouse","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-26T20:19:59Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"7dacbc886b848598aa139cb27ed80ce2ea630f90","github_link":"https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/commit/7dacbc886b848598aa139cb27ed80ce2ea630f90","commit_subject":"Address review: compare the month bucket offset in whole seconds","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"elizaOS/eliza","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-26T20:19:30Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"890410760bc197257dc